# FINAL SELF-CHECK

Before returning the JSON, verify internally:

* Every component mentioned in the transcript has exactly one entry and exactly one status —
  never invented, never omitted, never left blank.
* Every stated connection touching at least one non-`unchanged`-confirmed component has its own
  data contract candidate, one per direction, `name: "unknown"` when unnamed — never skipped
  just because it wasn't phrased as a contract, and never skipped for a component whose status
  is still `unknown`.
* No component or contract name appears that is not literally present in `TRANSCRIPT`.
* No producer, consumer, action, or status was inferred from a name or from what a component
  "usually" does — only from what was actually stated.
